# 19. OPERATIONAL DATA REFRESH POLICY

Implement source-specific scheduled jobs.

Possible scheduling architecture:

- Weather observations and forecasts: refresh according to provider cadence and operational usefulness.
- IMD warnings: refresh frequently enough to detect updated bulletins, respecting provider limits.
- GPM Early Run: check for newly available eligible granules.
- SMAP L4: check for newly published valid archive data rather than repeatedly requesting unavailable records.
- NASA POWER: refresh according to product availability and the requested date range.
- Landsat: periodically discover newly published scenes for the field.
- AGMARKNET: refresh when new daily market records become available.
- Soil tests: update only when a new verified report is submitted.
- Crop knowledge: review when a new official publication/version appears.

Do not use a single identical refresh interval for every provider.

Do not exceed provider access and rate limits.

Implement manual refresh where relevant.

Implement scheduled ingestion, retries and alerts for failures.

Use the observation timestamp rather than the retrieval time as the actual observation date.

